n Course\") in blue (#1A73E8). Rows contain user data with checkboxes, some selected, showing email addresses, last login times, join dates, purchase values in black text, and message icon buttons on the right. The font for table content is a clean sans-serif, size around 14px with normal weight. At the bottom, there is pagination info in grey, an upgrade link highlighted in black text, and a knowledge base message with a blue link. The layout uses a two-column design: a fixed narrow left side navigation and a wide main content area with consistent padding and margins, aligned left for text and centered for main content. The UI employs subtle lines and spacing to separate rows and columns, minimalistic icons, and a modern, professional style with a clear visual hierarchy. There are no animations visible in the screenshot.\n- **Layout**: The layout is a two-column design with a fixed vertical sidebar navigation on the left and a main content area occupying the majority of the screen on the right. The sidebar is narrow and vertically aligned with icons and text links stacked top-to-bottom, separated into groups under 'Users' heading. The main content side is a single flexible column containing the page header at top, followed by a horizontal toolbar with action buttons aligned right, then a filter/search section arranged horizontally, and lastly a data table with multiple rows and columns beneath it. Table columns include checkboxes, action dropdown, and key data fields arranged horizontally with headings aligned centrally or left. Spacing is generous with padding around buttons and input fields. Footer info and links appear below the table area. Overall, the layout keywords include: fixed sidebar, vertical navigation, single main content column, horizontal toolbar, horizontal filter/search row, data table with rows and columns, consistent margins and padding, aligned left text, and clear visual grouping.\n- **Functions**: On this interface, users can perform multiple detailed actions related to managing student records. They can filter the student list by using the 'Add Filter' dropdown and search for specific students by name or email via the search bar. Users can select one or more students using the checkboxes, enabling bulk actions through the 'Bulk Actions' dropdown, such as enrolling students in courses, unenrolling, sending emails, or adding tags. The presence of an 'Add Students' button allows adding new student accounts. Buttons for 'Export CSV' and 'Email Students' support exporting data and mass communication. The table shows detailed data entries including email status, login times, join dates, and purchase totals, providing both overview and detailed control. The interface facilitates efficient student management workflows like tracking student activity, communication, enrollment control, data export, and account additions. Overall, it enables administrative users to efficiently organize, contact, and manage their student base with clarity, flexibility, and ease of use through well-organized data presentation and interactive controls.\n\n### Site\n- **ID**: 358\n- **Name**:  Teachable\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/websites/358\n- **Domain**: teachable.com\n- **Categories**: Business\n- **Description**: Sell Courses, Coaching and Digital Downloads\n\n### Flows\n- **Creating tag** (Step 3 of 6, Flow ID: 9614)"
